    <!-- About -->
    <string name="about_org_name">Singapore Taiwan Student Association</string>
    <string name="about_purpose">Why we exist</string>
    <string name="about_purpose_1">Universities around the world have Taiwanese Student Associations. In most countries a TSA works directly with the local Taipei Representative Office, giving Taiwanese students a first point of contact, a faster route to settling in, and a network to lean on. We wanted to bring that to Singapore — but local policy prevents universities from recognising student societies formed around a nationality or ethnicity.</string>
    <string name="about_purpose_2">So we founded the Singapore Taiwanese Student Association instead: to connect Taiwanese students far from home, run events that bring them together, and share Taiwanese food and culture in Singapore — with students from anywhere welcome to join us.</string>
    <string name="about_purpose_3">The logo takes WWTSA\'s two colours as its starting point: an ocean-blue Formosan black bear for the island itself and the tie students keep to it, and a deep red lion\'s head for Singapore and the determination of studying far from home.</string>
    <string name="about_goals">Our goals</string>
    <string name="about_goal_1">Build and sustain a network for Taiwanese students in Singapore.</string>
    <string name="about_goal_2">Help students settle into life and culture in Singapore.</string>
    <string name="about_goal_3">Share Taiwanese culture with students from everywhere else.</string>
    <string name="about_wwtsa">WWTSA</string>
    <string name="about_wwtsa_body">STSA is a chapter of the World Wide Taiwanese Student Association, a global body serving Taiwanese students overseas and the TSAs they belong to, with a wider public-service mission back home.</string>
    <string name="about_wwtsa_link">WWTSA website</string>
